tery of the blue spider lily  and the creation  of the demon race the blue spider lily  is the reason why muzon became a demon  in the first place  and as such it is the key ingredient to  creating the entire  demon race the blue spider lily also  appears  in the very last chapter of the demon  slayer manga  so if there is any form of sequel to the  story which is highly likely in my  opinion because demon slayer has been  insanely profitable the blue spider lily  will play an important role in that  sequel so what do we really know about  this mysterious and extremely important  plant  muzon the first known demon and the  daddy of all the other demons  was born over 1 000 years ago as a very  sickly child  he was diagnosed with a terminal disease  that was expected to kill him before he  reached the age of 20.  since muzon was part of a wealthy family  they brought in doctors from across  japan  in an attempt to treat muzon's illness  one doctor in particular gave muzon a  highly experimental  and untested medicine whose main  ingredient was the mythical flower  known as the blue spider lily initially  the medicine didn't seem to have  any effect and this enraged muzon  he became so angry that he ended up  killing the doctor who gave him the  medicine  however after he had already killed the  doctor  muzan realized that the medicine was  having an effect it had just been  delayed  the medicine gave muzon an incredibly  strong body  and it made him virtually immortal he no  longer had to worry about dying before  reaching the age of 20  in fact he would live for over a  thousand years  but because this medicine was so  experimental and because it wasn't  finished  there were serious side effects first  muzon would have to kill and eat other  humans to survive  second muzon could never go out in the  sun  now that the medicine had turned muzon  into a demon  direct contact with the sun would kill  him  muzon wasn't exactly a compassionate guy  to begin with  after all he literally killed the doctor  who was trying to save his life because  he got mad  so for musan the idea of devouring  humans to survive  wasn't a major issue but the idea of  having to hide from the sun for all of  eternity  was a big problem and muzon spent the  rest of his life  trying to figure out a way to conquer  the sun and become  the perfect being muzon came to regret  killing the doctor who gave him the  medicine  because if the doctor had lived he may  have been able to improve the medicine  and make it possible for muzan to go out  in the sun  but since the doctor was already dead he  would never be able to complete  this experimental medicine and this  meant that muzon would have to find a  way to conquer the sun  on his own muzon firmly believed that  finding this mythical blue spider lily  would be crucial for his plan to conquer  the sun  which would in turn allow him to become  the perfect being  and so he spent centuries searching  throughout japan  for this special flower unfortunately  for him  he was never able to find it he  subsequently created many other demons  in the hopes that one of them would be  able to help him find a way to conquer  the sun  and he eventually switched the focus of  his search from the blue spider lily to  nezuko kamado  because nezuko had somehow succeeded in  conquering the sun  despite being a demon so at this point  we might be thinking that the blue  spider lily  is extinct or that it is no longer  relevant to the story  but then in chapter 205 of the demon  slayer manga  the final chapter of the entire series  aopa hashibira the modern day descendant  of inosuke hashibira  discovers several samples of the blue  spider lily  alba is the great grandson ominosuke and  a famous botanist who figured out that  the blue spider lily  only blooms during the day for two or  three days of the year  this incredibly specific and short  blooming period  is likely part of the reason why the  blue spider lily is so hard  to find however due to some unspecified  mistake by alba  all the blue spider lilies that he had  discovered withered away  this implies that these particular  flowers are no longer a threat  in terms of turning someone into a demon  but  the fact that these blue spider lilies  were discovered in the first place  means that the demon threat may not be  over after all if alba could discover  multiple blue spider lilies in modern  times  then clearly these mythical flowers are  still around  they didn't just go extinct a thousand  years ago or something like that  and if they are still around then there  is always the possibility that someone  else will use them to become a demon  either by accident or because they  somehow learned  the truth about the blue spider lily's  mysterious properties  now if the mangakao demon slayer wanted  us to think that the demons were already  gone forever  she probably wouldn't have included the  blue spider lily  in the final chapter after all since  muzon spent  over a thousand years looking for this  mythical plant and could never find it  it would have been very easy for us to  believe that the flower just went  extinct at some point and so it could  never be used to create a demon again  but the mangaka specifically chose to  include  the blue spider lily in the final  chapter and to make it known to us that  it still exists  out there somewhere even in the modern  world  this opens the door for a possible new  demon threat  emerging sometime in the future it is a  remote possibility to be sure  but it's still a possibility as long as  the blue spider lily  is still out there somewhere more demons  could appear  and that means that new demon slayer  content could also appear  and who knows maybe new demons did  appear in the past  already but they've just remained hidden  or maybe they are located in  other countries i've always wondered  what was going on  outside of japan in the demon slayer  world  muzon was obviously japanese but it's  certainly possible that over the past  thousand years some of the demons from  japan moved to other countries  and in fact it's possible that someone  outside of japan  also found out about the blue spider  lily so there could be other muzons  out there in the world the blue spider  lily is a mythical flower  but it is based on the real flower known  as the red  spider lily in japanese folklore the red  spider lily is associated with death and  reincarnation  so it's interesting that the blue spider  lily is associated with the opposite  immortality and eternal life but  at a cost now in the real world the red  spider lily can be found  in other countries not just in japan  so it's possible that the same is true  about the blue spider lily  in the world of demon slayer the blue  spider lily is obviously much more rare  than its red counterpart  but when we're talking about a time span  of thousands of years  there is certainly a possibility that  someone somewhere else in the world  also found this flower and used it for a  purpose  similar to musons at the end of the day  this series is called  demon slayer so if there are no demons  to slay  there is no story since muzon is now  dead  if there is a sequel or any form of  continuation to  this series and judging by how insanely  profitable the series has been  a continuation is very likely in my  opinion then we can be certain that the  blue spider lily  is going to play an important role in  the new story  and personally i can't wait to find out  more  about this incredibly mysterious and  interesting flower  let me know what you guys think what is  the secret of the blue spider lily  and how is it able to transform humans  into demons  do you think that there are other blue  spider lilies out there somewhere  maybe even in other countries finally if  there is a continuation to the demon  slayer story  who do you think will be the villain  will it be some kind of prequel with  muzon as the villain once ag